      "id": 1,
      "text": "Claude was originally called Armstrong City, but the name changed in 1887 to honor engineer Claude Ayers who brought the first train through.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/claude-tx",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first train of the Fort Worth and Denver Railway passed through the area in 1887, marking the town’s birth as a rail hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/claude-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Claude’s courthouse, built in 1912, still stands as the centerpiece of the town’s historic downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude%2C_Texas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Armstrong County Museum in Claude showcases local history and Western-themed exhibits that tell the story of the Panhandle.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude%2C_Texas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Three classic films—Hud, The Sundowners, and Sunshine Christmas—were shot in Claude, giving the town a place in Hollywood history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude%2C_Texas",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "When Armstrong County formed in 1890, Claude and Washburn vied for the county seat, a contest that ultimately crowned Claude.",
